### Build entry point (mandatory)

All Docker-based builds and CI-parity verification use **Taskfile** from the repository root:

```bash
task <target>    # ✅ always this
```

**Never** run `docker buildx bake`, `docker buildx build`, or `docker build` directly in agent shells.  
Implementation detail lives in `docker-bake.hcl` + `meta-secret/Dockerfile`; **Taskfile.yml is the only entry point.**

**Skill:** [`.ai/skills/build-via-task/SKILL.md`](../../skills/build-via-task/SKILL.md) — mapping table, exceptions, pre-command checklist.

### Exceptions

| Context | Allowed |
|---------|---------|
| Single-crate Rust | `cargo test/build -p …` from `meta-secret/` |
| web-cli UI only (no Docker/WASM) | `bun run …` in `meta-secret/web-cli/ui/` |
| Adding a new build target | Edit `Taskfile.yml` first, then `task <target>` |

After any `Cargo.toml` change: `task generate-recipe`.

### Task commands

| Action | Command |
|---|---|
| Run tests (CI parity) | `task test` |
| Build native Rust workspace (release gate) | `task rust-build-release` |
| Rust workspace lint/security gate | `task rust-clippy` |
| Rust coverage gate (>=80%) | `task rust-coverage` |
| Local regular Rust tests (32 MiB test-stack setting) | `task rust-test` |
| Warm Rust test deps image | `task warm-cache` |
| Warm WASM deps image | `task warm-cache-wasm` |
| Build all images | `task build` |
| Build + push | `task push` |
| Build meta-server | `task meta-server` |
| Apple infra unit/config/syntax | `task apple-infra-test`, `task apple-config-check`, `task apple-infra-syntax` |
| Real offline Cloudflared/KCL | `CLOUDFLARED_BIN=… KCL_BIN=… task apple-tunnel-check` |
| Apple-only ignored exports / KCL | `task apple-prepare`, `task apple-render` (explicit profile pointers) |
| Owned local HTTP smoke | `task apple-local-smoke` (free3000; no accounts/tunnel) |
| Changed taskomatic image | `task taskomatic`, then `task apple-taskomatic-offline` |
| Explicit future server push | `task meta-server-push` (separate authorization required) |
| Build web image | `task web` |
| Export web dist locally | `task web-local` |
| Export wasm pkg locally | `task wasm-local` |
| Update cargo chef recipe | `task generate-recipe` |
| Run web-ui locally | `task web-run` |
| Playwright smoke tests | `PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=… task playwright-test` |
| Add shadcn-vue component | `cd meta-secret/web-cli/ui && npx shadcn-vue@latest add <name>` |

List all targets: `task -l` from repo root.

### Android native layout gate

From Core root, `task android-native-test` runs the focused stdlib ELF/ZIP fixture bank.
`task android-native-coverage -- /absolute/run-artifacts/coverage` runs the same
bank through stdlib trace with count/summary/missing-line reports. With no argument,
reports go to `.ai/artifacts/run/android-native-coverage`; no .cover files go beside
source. Record verifier-specific statement coverage separately from imported stdlib
files. This reruns the focused bank and does not measure Rust/native/UI coverage.
`task android-native-verify -- --role app /absolute/app.apk` requires exactly one
own library for arm64-v8a, armeabi-v7a and x86_64; `--role instrumentation` permits
zero native entries. `--abi arm64-v8a /absolute/library.so` checks a standalone ELF.
All packaged native paths are scanned, including legacy x86/armeabi/MIPS/MIPS64;
only arm64-v8a and x86_64 require16KiB PT_LOAD alignment. Stored ZIP data alignment
is separate from ELF alignment; compressed entries explicitly have no mmap verdict.
Report errors block acceptance. No permissive invalid-ELF mode exists.

After old immutable artifact semantic RED and source review, Root may run
`task android-native-build`: this invokes existing Android script, installs Rust
targets, builds three mobile archives, regenerates Kotlin and copies native files
directly into sibling Compose. Serialize with runtime/build ownership. Preserve
old provenance; new binaries require a new generation. Independent owning NDK
readelf and SDK zipalign on actual signed APKs, exported ABI/dependency/UniFFI
identity, byte-identical generated Kotlin, NX/WX/GNU_RELRO baseline comparison
and genuine native runtime gates remain necessary. A verifier pass is no UI E2E
acceptance. No unrelated full Rust suite is implied by a shell-only layout fix.
